      "score": 93,
      "summary": "Each finding has its own evidence, unknowns, repair steps and acceptance check, which makes the fixes the most ready to implement. It gives specific provisional performance gates: p95 latency, long tasks, a mounted-row bound, heap growth and regression tolerances. Hostile-data and upload handling is strong, including not implying an unfinished upload was stored. It treats static signals as contextual under design-system authority and gives explicit rollback/hold conditions."
