      "score": 90,
      "summary": "A strong audit whose failure-to-recovery table clearly covers 401, 403, 409, 429, 500/timeout, offline and partial-batch failures. It covers hostile data well, including bidirectional text and rendering names as text, and gives careful touch-target and WCAG nuance. It reconciles static signals cleanly. Its performance budgets are only partly specific, with a tolerance that is defined later, and its acceptance conditions are less tied to individual findings than B's."
